# Keeping these out is not just about build speed: copying host node_modules into
# the image would break pnpm's symlink layout, and copying .env would bake local
# development secrets into a published image.
node_modules
**/node_modules

dist
**/dist
build
**/build
.turbo
**/.turbo
**/generated

# Patterns are anchored at the context root, so the ** forms matter: without them
# infra/.env — the file holding the production secrets — would land in a layer.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

.git
.github
.vscode
.idea

*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage
**/coverage

README.md
infra/README.md
